Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(spec):=20concat=20exclusion=20detector=20(?=
 =?UTF-8?q?AC=20+=20classe-costante)=20con=20selftest=20parit=C3=A0=20[t8?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20branch-2]?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Chunk 2 runtime, task 5: the two-signal pattern-window detector of the
branch-2 plan lands in C++ as a header-only library, with the Python
reference (scripts/t8-b2-detector.py in the workspace) staying the
certified semantics - parity is pinned by a fixture selftest (gate G1).
No round wiring here: the per-round exclusion is the next task.

- common/spec-concat-exclusion.h: namespace spec_concat_exclusion with
  the pre-registered constants (W=16, P_MIN=2, P_MAX=8, THETA_AC=0.6,
  M=4, spec section 4.5) and the pure functions score_ac /
  has_constant_class / gating (sections 4.1-4.3). Token-compare only:
  the AC decision uses the integer form match*10 > (n-p)*6, exactly
  equivalent to the Python float form match/(n-p) > 0.6 for every
  reachable (match, denominator) pair (verified exhaustively up to
  w=16 in the plan review - documented in the header). Strict > (the
  0.6-exact knife-edge is NOT gated), class scan starts at i=r+p so
  the index r < p stays out of the class (section 4.2).
- tests/spec-concat-exclusion-fixtures.json: the parity contract - 200
  windows with the expected (gated, segnale): the 8 test-file witness
  windows (real copy-mode geometries, knife-edge tk, w-border, short)
  + 184 corpus-b2 windows (92 gated + 92 non-gated len-16, 4+4 len-24
  pinning the evaluate-whole contract), deterministic scan-order
  sampling (no RNG), regenerated by --dump-fixtures.
- common.h/arg.cpp: --spec-concat-exclusion (default enabled,
  effective while concat_k1 > 0; --no- re-exposes copy-mode) and
  --spec-concat-selftest FNAME, plumbed like --spec-concat-k1.
- server: server_spec_concat_selftest() parses the fixtures (nlohmann,
  vendored) and checks gating on every window; called from main()
  right after arg parsing - pre-load by construction: no backend init,
  no HTTP, no model, exit code 0 on PASS n/n. Boot marker next to the
  concat guard reports the exclusion state (WARNING when disabled on a
  configured concat mode).

G1 (host harness, same logic): PASS 200/200 exit 0; mutated knife-edge
fixture -> FAIL 199/200 exit 1. Container run on the dedicated image
tag in the task log.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai <glm@z.ai>
